<title>THAILAND: Union Bank plans to double capital.</title>
<headline>Union Bank plans to double capital.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Union Bank of Bangkok Plc said on Thursday it plans to double its paid-up capital to 1.6 billion baht ($64 million) from 800 million.</p>
<p>Union Bank said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand that its board of directors will later this week consider details on the planned capital hike.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 25 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
